Day 2: AI vs ML vs Deep Learning
AI: Artificial Intelligence
AI is a large term.
It can include simple if else rules. This is also known as symbolic AI or an expert system.
Expert system means we take knowledge from an expert, like a chess player, and write code using that knowledge.
But an expert system works only for a specific problem. In this case, it works only for chess.
It does not work well with fuzzy data.
ML: Machine Learning
ML works with fuzzy data.
It finds patterns. We do not write the rules.
It uses statistics and math tools.
Deep Learning
Deep learning is a part of machine learning.
In ML, we define the features.
Example:
For a dog and cat image classifier, we may give features like:
Ears up = dog
Ears down = cat
Long tail = dog
But in deep learning, it detects the features by itself.
Deep learning is inspired by our biology.
It is best for fuzzy data.
If we have very large data, we use deep learning. But most of the time, we use ML.

